  "notes": "Planned as three blocks stepping back from the street - the drawing room and the porch in front, the dining room and hall behind them, the kitchen wing behind that - on a corridor running through. Read off the plate, the lobbies are the point of the plan: there are three on the ground floor and one upstairs, and every one of them sits between a served room and a serving one. The dining room is not entered from the corridor directly but through a lobby; the scullery and larder hang off a lobby rather than off the kitchen; the water closet and the coals open off a third, reached past the china closet and never through the kitchen. The two principal rooms do not communicate.",
